<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alps</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Alps are the major mountain range of south-central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, separating <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibals-crossing-of-the-alps">Hannibal's crossing of the Alps</a> with an army and elephants in 218 BCE is one of the most famous episodes of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punic-empire">Punic Empire</a>'s wars with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. Centuries later, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a> crossed them to conquer the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> kingdom, extending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a> into Italy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alps.jpg" alt="Alps" width="320" height="249" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Terra (EOS AM-1) satellite · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alps_2007-03-13_10.10UTC_1px-250m.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
